<title>SOUTH KOREA: Korean Air raises domestic air fares.</title>
<headline>Korean Air raises domestic air fares.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-07-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Korean Airlines Co said on Friday it had decided to raise domestic air fares by an average of 19 percent from August 11.</p>
<p>A company statement said it was forced to raise fares in order to cover a huge foreign exchange translation loss following the Korean won's depreciation against the dollar.</p>
<p>The translation loss amounted to 108.9 billion won in the first five months of this year and 129.7 billion won in 1996.</p>
<p>--Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5643</p>
</text>
